#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:5
#: ca53f55fa3294f96b0f77125079c15fa
msgid "Traditional Helicopter Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:7
#: 10dd81bd935642e08da8efacc68ac784
msgid "Be sure to follow the wiki instructions, step by step!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:8
#: 9d1d677b045646bbaa4b5af1d0c03947
msgid "Be sure the CG is in line with the main rotor shaft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:9
#: 7670d3a0f13d4577b8a243bf5484473b
msgid "Blade tracking must be within a quarter blade thickness or better to avoid excessive vibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:10
#: 18a80809f7d94156ae5f223ca1e91af3
msgid "Vibration is the arch enemy of Helicopter autopilots!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:11
#: 84fa26464457478bad87ae6e70751f34
msgid "Internal Combustion Engines and Turbines can created high frequency vibrations that do not appear in the VIBE logs and can be aliased to low frequencies which can impact EKF and Attitude control (see below for ground tests to check for this). This also often occurs in electric helicopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:12
#: 72fb29ae454541ad9fe7cd9dd781319f
msgid "The autopilot should be well isolated for vibration. Using autopilots with internal IMU vibration damping and vibration reducing mounts is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:13
#: 41bbc52cd40a49e980da6ddf1ccec89c
msgid "Traditional Helicopter *is* capable of inverted flight and using full negative collective ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:16
#: 43c97f1ed2b745e0b44dc6d242ae223f
msgid "Checking for High Frequency Vibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:18
#: 84157a96c4cc4d03af8f653291d6f53f
msgid "High frequency vibrations in this context are vibrations close to the IMU sampling frequency, or its multiples, which will be aliased down into the same range as control inputs for the attitude controllers. Symptoms of high frequency vibration can be that the attitude estimate becomes incorrect causing it to lean significantly even though the pilot is commanding level flight in stabilized modes. In the extreme, it can result in an :ref:`ekf-inav-failsafe` or even a crash. Excessive vibration can also make altitude hold imprecise or even produce uncontrollable climbs/descents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:20
#: 8e2fa6964b8b41cf916cf97c9bc572b8
msgid "One method of testing this, is to secure the helicopter to the ground, and run up the main rotor, watching the artificial horizon in the ground control station. If it moves away from level, you probably have a vibration issue which needs to be addressed. Testing should be done at various collective levels and rotor speeds. Be careful not to over-stress the helicopter with collective extremes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:22
#: 3f8f9cbbc32041f49b254fa44fe45bed
msgid "Setup for ground test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:24
#: 60d9ee402e1747299316ea5ea2dfb619
msgid "Secure vehicle to the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:25
#: dd1bdc7cd94b4b5fbc4cc06308f94919
msgid "Temporarily reduce Roll, Pitch, and Yaw  P,I,and D, PIDs to zero. Be sure to restore them after this test!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:26
#: 3e96f0d304f141a385d59b49b8d04847
msgid "Set :ref:`ACRO_OPTIONS<ACRO_OPTIONS>` = 2, temporarily, if not being used already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:27
#: b57d3d3193c54cad82b63a3fb06cb0db
msgid "Change to ACRO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:28
#: 11080448e4b144f7b67d28c326d93d0a
msgid "Arm and engage motor interlock, allowing the vehicle to spool up at 0 degree pitch, watching for any change from level in the GSC of the artificial horizon. Any significant tilt indicates noise is disrupting the attitude estimate and should be investigated and eliminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:29
#: 315961a2b870438a8eaab95d801fb104
msgid "Change the target main rotor speed a bit above and below the nominal target using the :ref:`H_RSC_SETPOINT<H_RSC_SETPOINT>` (or TX throttle curve if using Passthru mode) and repeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:30
#: 06ea13a45fe346e9a74894f4b04b5595
msgid "Re-check the blade tracking also while doing this test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:32
#: 89a49036c49f48769a0c20864633f67d
msgid "Be sure to also eliminate the possibility of lower frequency vibrations from the main or tail rotors causing the issue. Unlike vibrations near the sampling rate and its harmonics, which cannot be eliminated by software filtering, rotor vibrations can be improved using ArduPilot's notch filtering feature. See :ref:`common-measuring-vibration` and :ref:`Helicopter Dynamic Notch Filter Setup<common-imu-notch-filtering-helicopter-setup>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:35
#: c87ba666f35044918f62cdf959d61c84
msgid "Possible False Landing Detections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:37
#: ed50ff09fb964df091b4dde2420e6404
msgid "Under extreme circumstances (flying in extremely turbulent conditions, for example), it is possible for the firmware, to falsely detect a landing condition, although still flying. This can lead to lack of control in position control modes and even possible disarming. An RC Auxiliary Function (\"159\") is provided to allow an RC to enable (needed when actually landing) or disable (to prevent false detects during missions) the landing detection algorithm under pilot control."
msgstr ""
